# Keep `.brain` in sync with code changes

When a change affects documented architecture, APIs, data models, or product concepts, update the relevant `.brain` file in the same session. Don't leave the brain stale.

## When to update

- New or removed CLI command / HTTP endpoint
- Post kind, contract shape, or Zod schema change
- Storage schema change (new table, column, or tier rule)
- Package rename, split, or new dependency
- Naming or terminology change (e.g. a concept is renamed)
- A phase/task in the brain is completed

## Key mappings

| Changed area | Brain file(s) to check |
|---|---|
| `packages/khora/host/`, `apps/khora/server/` | `technical/host.md`, `technical/colonnade.md` |
| `packages/khora/relay-colonnade/` | `technical/colonnade.md`, `technical/id-conventions.md` |
| `packages/colonnade/` | `technical/colonnade.md` |
| `packages/khora/contracts/` — post kinds, subscription shapes | `product/khora.md`, `technical/percolator.md` |
| `packages/obp/`, `apps/vellum/` | `technical/obp-protocol.md`, `product/vellum.md`, `technical/vellum-rooms.md` |
| `packages/memories/` | `product/memories.md` |
| `packages/registry/`, `apps/khoralabs/registry/` | `product/registry.md`, `technical/registry.md`, `technical/onboarding-flow.md` |
| `apps/khora/cli/` — new commands | `technical/host.md` (CLI surface section) |
| Percolator / subscription fan-out | `technical/percolator.md` |

## What to do

1. Read the relevant brain file before finishing your changes.
2. Update any stale descriptions, add new commands/endpoints/types, mark completed roadmap items with `[x]`.
3. If a concept is renamed everywhere in code, rename it in the brain too.

The brain is the source of truth for **what things are and why** — not a mirror of every implementation detail. Update the concepts, not the line numbers.
